Z||000000||Taijiguy||05-23-2001||03:03 PM||||...or at least, the smartest one I've run across yet:<BR>A couple of kids in a riced out Acura with fartcan exhaust tip and no profile tires and wheels. I pull up next to him at a light. The light changes, and I had no real intention of racing. But then I hear him start to wind it out a bit, so I fed my carb a bit more gas. The rest of this happens very fast: I move up and the passenger gets a glimpse of my shaker scoop; a very painicked look crosses his face. He nudges the driver but still he continues to wind it out. I'm still in first, so I decide it's time to make a statement. I slip the clutch, let the r's come up to about 4,500, let go of the clutch, and pour on the gas. This of course causes me to get something of a bark out of the tires (OK, maybe even it gets me a wee bit sideways, but you never heard that from me)At that point, Mr.Backwardshatriceboy realizes he's completely outgunned. He's brought a Nerf bat to a gunfight. He shuts it down and forgets any thoughts of glory he may have had. No doubt the smartest move he made all day...<BR>Oh how I love this car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
